# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-001

1. In `pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/domain/models/SourceValidationModels.scala`, create the complete file below. It defines status and record types and the circe codecs used by the manifest reader and result store. `checkedAtMillis` and `generatedAtMillis` are Long epoch milliseconds so no Java-time codec is needed.



```scala

package newspipe.domain.models



import io.circe.Decoder

import io.circe.Encoder

import io.circe.generic.semiauto.deriveDecoder

import io.circe.generic.semiauto.deriveEncoder



enum ValidationStatus:

  case Usable, TemporarilyUnavailable, Invalid, NeedsInvestigation



final case class SourceCandidate(

    publisherId: String,

    title: Option[String],

    provenance: Option[String],

    urls: List[String]

)



final case class ProbeResponse(

    statusCode: Int,

    finalUrl: String,

    contentType: String,

    body: String

)



final case class FeedValidation(

    url: String,

    status: ValidationStatus,

    reason: String,

    checkedAtMillis: Long,

    detail: String,

    feedType: Option[String],

    entryCount: Int,

    hasDates: Boolean,

    hasIds: Boolean

)



final case class CandidateReport(candidate: SourceCandidate, validations: List[FeedValidation])



final case class ValidationSnapshot(

    version: Int,

    generatedAtMillis: Long,

    reports: List[CandidateReport]

)



object SourceValidationModels:

  given Encoder[ValidationStatus] = Encoder.encodeString.contramap(_.toString)

  given Decoder[ValidationStatus] = Decoder.decodeString.emap { value =>

    ValidationStatus.values.find(_.toString == value).toRight("unknown validation status: " + value)

  }

  given Encoder[SourceCandidate] = deriveEncoder

  given Decoder[SourceCandidate] = deriveDecoder

  given Encoder[FeedValidation] = deriveEncoder

  given Decoder[FeedValidation] = deriveDecoder

  given Encoder[CandidateReport] = deriveEncoder

  given Decoder[CandidateReport] = deriveDecoder

  given Encoder[ValidationSnapshot] = deriveEncoder

  given Decoder[ValidationSnapshot] = deriveDecoder

```



Prove: `cd pipelines/ingestion && sbt compile` prints `[success] Compiled` and no error about SourceValidationModels.



Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/application/ports/Ports.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/**, pipelines/ingestion/src/test/**, conf/**, scripts/**, pipelines/enrichment/**



Stop when the model file compiles; the port additions belong to the next step.



2. In `pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/application/ports/Ports.scala`, replace the import line and append exactly the four traits below after `trait ObjectStoreReadinessProbe`. Keep `RssSource`, `BronzeSink`, `RawPublisher`, `ProbeResult` and `DependencyProbe` byte-identical.



```scala

import newspipe.domain.models.{BronzeUnit, FeedValidation, ProbeResponse, RssItem, SourceCandidate, ValidationSnapshot}



trait SourceManifestReader:

  def read(path: String): Either[String, List[SourceCandidate]]



trait FeedProbe:

  def probe(url: String): Either[String, ProbeResponse]



trait FeedValidator:

  def validate(candidate: SourceCandidate, response: ProbeResponse, nowMillis: Long): FeedValidation

  def discover(body: String): Option[String]



trait ValidationResultStore:

  def load(): Either[String, Option[ValidationSnapshot]]

  def save(snapshot: ValidationSnapshot): Either[String, Unit]

```



Prove: `cd pipelines/ingestion && sbt compile` prints `[success] Compiled`; `grep -c 'trait SourceManifestReader' pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/application/ports/Ports.scala` prints `1`.



Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/application/services/IngestionService.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/control/dependencyInjection/AppContainer.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/control/entryPoint/Main.scala, pipelines/enrichment/**



Stop when both new files compile; adapter implementations are cu-002 through cu-005.
